\chapter{Schematic Design and Component Selection}

\section{Power Delivery Network (PDN)}
A typical PDN includes:
\begin{itemize}
\item Multi-phase buck converters for core voltages (0.7--0.85 V).
\item LDO regulators for noise-sensitive analog/RF rails.
\item PMICs with integrated sequencing logic.
\end{itemize}

\section{High-Speed Interfaces}
Key interfaces include USB4/Thunderbolt 4, 10GbE PHYs, MIPI CSI-2/DSI, and display protocols such as
eDP. Retimers and redrivers ensure signal integrity across long traces.

\section{Clocking and Timing}
Low-jitter crystal oscillators, TCXOs, and PLL-based clock generators maintain timing margins across
temperature and voltage variations.

